    "answer": {
      "short": "$LM=NM$.",
      "worked": "As L and N are midpoints, $BL=\\frac{AB}{2}=\\frac{AC}{2}=CN$. Since M is the midpoint of BC, $BM=CM$. Also $\\angle LBM=\\angle NCM$, the base angles of the isosceles triangle ABC. Thus $\\triangle BLM\\cong\\triangle CNM$ by SAS. Corresponding sides give $LM=NM$.",
